  <data name="MapDescription" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The map is drawn on a canvas without external map APIs. The default is the equal-area Equal Earth projection; the older rectangular one is an option. Points are coloured by category, and the legend above the map hides and shows them. Nearby markers merge into groups with a counter: a click zooms into a group, and points with the same coordinates fan out. The data set and grouping change on the fly; changing the projection or meridian recreates the component. Points can be downloaded as GeoJSON, and you can load your own GeoJSON file, for example one drawn in geojson.io.</value>
